1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
<font color="#20e020">HI removed, cleaned
and corrected by Lunar Team</font>

2
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:27,109
What do we got?

3
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:30,946
Jim Gulbrand, CEO and founder
of the software company Gaia Matrix...

4
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,158
...was reported missing
by his live-in brother yesterday.

5
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:35,451
Local P.D. responded.

6
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:37,995
But they didn't check the boat
until this morning.

7
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,956
They found blood on the deck,
but no sign of a body.

8
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:42,207
Why is it ours?

9
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:45,502
The marina is privately owned,
on lease by the city of Sausalito.

10
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,297
It was local P.D.'s decision
whether to take the case.

11
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:51,467
High-profile missing-persons case?

12
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:54,470
Wonder why they wouldn't take that.

13
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:02,478
- You coming?
- He's not feeling well. Stomach.

14
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:03,645
I'm fine.

15
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:06,774
You get me sick, I'm gonna put you
on stake out for a month.

16
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:08,400
Yes, boss.

17
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:22,873
- This is it?
- Yeah.

18
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:25,667
- No sign of a struggle? No weapon?
- Nothing.

19
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,419
What else do we know?

20
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:31,048
Jim Gulbrand is 33 years old.
He lives here in Sausalito.

21
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:33,509
Has an estimated net worth
of $100 million.

22
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:35,594
- He's rich.
- Very rich.

23
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:39,014
He was also recently divorced
from one Kathryn Stubbs-Gulbrand.

24
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:41,016
Did the victim have a criminal record?

25
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:44,686
No. The company he founded,
Gaia Matrix...

26
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:48,065
...was under investigation
by the SEC for securities violations.

27
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,527
We're getting the paperwork now,
but, apparently...

28
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:55,322
...he was facing heavy fines
and federal prison time.

29
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,790
Oh, hey, do you need my help with...?

30
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,041
Never mind.

31
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,252
Maybe it's all just an elaborate hoax.

32
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,254
That would explain
why there's no body.

33
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:55,924
You take a boat out, everybody assumes
you're at the bottom of the ocean.

34
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:58,594
Your body and your killer
are never to be found.

35
00:02:58,761 --> 00:03:01,263
That would make perfect sense.

36
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,016
This one? No.

37
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:06,226
How about this one?

38
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:11,273
Sorry.

39
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:14,776
- What?
- No use in being anchored...

40
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:16,904
...when you're tied up at the dock.

41
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:22,284
Ah, after you.

42
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,586
When did you notice
your brother was missing?

43
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:18,048
Jim and I talked every day.
He didn't come home.

44
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:20,133
You live here with your brother, Keith?

45
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:22,177
For a few months. Semi-temporarily.

46
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:25,222
Jim wanted company
during his divorce.

47
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,641
After you, bro.

48
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:30,727
Tell us about your brother.

49
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:33,188
Who he associated with,
what drove him.

50
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:36,358
Well, Jim's life was Gaia Matrix, yeah.

51
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:38,694
That's the company he started
with Rick.

52
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:43,532
Green platform software.

53
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,200
Don't ask me what that is.

54
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:47,703
Rick being Rick Bregman?

55
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:51,707
Rick and Jim are best friends
from grade school.

56
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:54,710
And they built a whole empire
out of our parent's garage.

57
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:59,381
At the... At the time,
I was totally bummed, you know...

58
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,592
...because I'm like, "Dude,
where do I set up my drum kit now?"

59
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,636
Well.

60
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,388
Little did I know.

61
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:10,225
What about his personal life?
Was he dating anyone?

62
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,395
Brooke Harper. Cool woman.

63
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:14,938
For a psychiatrist.

64
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:18,400
- She's a psychiatrist?
- Yeah.

65
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:20,819
Works at the Sausalito Rehab Center.

66
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:22,487
I was in there for a...

67
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:25,574
...refresher course...

68
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:29,244
...and that's how they first met,
when Jim came to visit.

69
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:32,080
Did your brother and Brooke
have any arguments lately?

70
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:34,291
No. Jim was crazy about her.

71
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:38,211
He said she's the only woman
that could figure him out.

72
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:41,298
I think he was gonna propose to her.

73
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,467
Your brother was
recently divorced, right?

74
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:46,636
From a Kathryn Stubbs-Gulbrand?

75
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,930
Best thing he ever did.

76
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,601
That woman was a nightmare.

77
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,603
How so?

78
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:56,313
She was just a giant greed head.

79
00:05:56,481 --> 00:06:00,859
I mean, all she wanted was a
bigger house, bigger boat, more jewelry.

80
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:04,154
Do you play all these instruments?

81
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:06,114
Keyboards and bass, mostly.

82
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:09,326
Is it a sort of a new-age rock fusion?

83
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:12,621
Yeah. Kind of... Yeah.

84
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:15,374
You know, with an edge.
How did you know, man?

85
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:17,626
Wild guess.

86
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:19,795
Make much money
playing the keyboards?

87
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:22,547
No, but I'm not in it for the money.

88
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:26,051
You know, music's a...
It's a spiritual thing.

89
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,012
Yeah, it is. So is money.

90
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:32,057
Everything that exists
has a spiritual essence.

91
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:33,975
Or not at all.

92
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,478
So, what happens to all this?
Who gets it?

93
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:41,024
A portion of the estate will go
to the charities that Jim supported...

94
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:42,651
...and the rest will go to me.

95
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:44,403
Ah, motive.

96
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,321
Whoa.

97
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:50,158
- Chill, man.
- Oh, I'm just playing.

98
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:55,330
- Where were you Friday night?
- I...

99
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:58,375
...was in bed with a lady friend.

100
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:00,710
Gretchen something...

101
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,088
Number?

102
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:12,931
Thank you.

103
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:21,940
- What do you reckon?
- Possible.

104
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:23,525
- You?
- Not sure.

105
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,360
Cho, write down this number.

106
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:26,903
555-0139.

107
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:29,197
- Got it.
- Gretchen. No last name.

108
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:31,783
It's the brother's alibi
for last Friday night.

109
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,076
Have Van Pelt check it.

110
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:36,246
You and Rigsby go and talk
to Gulbrand's partner Rick Bregman.

111
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:40,333
- He should be at Gaia Matrix.
- All right. Will do, boss.

112
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:42,919
Rigsby.

113
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:45,881
What?

114
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:49,968
Never mind.

115
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:05,233
Agent Cho.
This is Agent Van Pelt. CBI.

116
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:07,402
Stuart Hansen. I'll take you to Rick.

117
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,489
- Right.
- What's your job here, Mr. Hansen?

118
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:12,949
Jim hates labels and pigeonholes.

119
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:16,620
I'm kind of the security chief,
but that sounds so fascistic, doesn't it?

120
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:22,918
What I am, really, is the firewalls and
encryptions and off-the-wall ideas guy.

121
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:29,007
Rick's been in the conference room
all morning dealing with the fallout.

122
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,760
He's pretty broken up. We all are.

123
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:36,640
Jim meant so much to this company.
To all of us.

124
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:45,023
The company is co-owned by you
and Jim, is that right?

125
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,901
- Yes.
- How did that relationship work?

126
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:52,113
Jim was the creative brain
behind Gaia Matrix.

127
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:53,949
He was the visionary.

128
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:55,492
I handled the business side.

129
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:57,452
We made a good team.

130
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:01,915
He was a genius,
but he wasn't aggressive.

131
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,626
Me, I'm a jock. Competitive.

132
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:06,962
I like to win. Make no apologies for it.

133
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:10,131
Is that what got you into trouble
with the SEC?

134
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:13,468
My lawyers warned me this line
of questioning might come up.

135
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:16,638
This is all I'm prepared to say
on that subject at the moment:

136
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:21,017
I am currently under investigation
by the SEC for securities violations...

137
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:25,021
- ...due to my role here at Gaia Matrix.
- Doesn't sound like you said anything.

138
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:28,066
You understand
why I can't comment any further.

139
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:31,695
Did the investigation cause
any animosity between you and Jim?

140
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:33,154
No.

141
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:34,990
Not at all. We were like brothers.

142
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:37,867
- Where were you the night of his murder?
- Home. Alone.

143
00:09:38,035 --> 00:09:40,662
Look, you're not getting this.

144
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:43,999
Jim was the creative genius
behind Gaia Matrix.

145
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:48,545
Without him,
this company is in grave jeopardy.

146
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:53,466
I had nothing to gain
and everything to lose by his death.

147
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:02,726
Dr. Harper, how long had you been
dating Jim Gulbrand?

148
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:07,606
It was just after I transferred here
from Boston, so seven months ago now.

149
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:12,027
His... An acquaintance
of his was staying here...

150
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:14,863
- We hit it off right away.
- Can you think of anyone who...

151
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,574
Excuse me. Might want him dead?

152
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:20,702
I've thought about that
a lot this morning and...

153
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,370
...I can't think of anyone.

154
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,916
Jim was a kind, gentle,
generous, brilliant man.

155
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:30,920
I can't imagine anyone being capable
of doing something so awful to him.

156
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,882
Really? You're a psychiatrist
and you can't imagine that?

157
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:38,303
To be more precise, I can't imagine
a rational reason for wishing him dead.

158
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,723
It's standard procedure to ask.

159
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:44,059
Where were you on
the night of the murder?

160
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:46,895
I was here, finishing up some work.

161
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:49,272
I can have the admin nurse...

162
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,816
...send over the paperwork
documenting my hours.

163
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,611
Yeah, that would be helpful,
thank you.

164
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:58,114
Do you have any leads
on the investigation so far?

165
00:10:58,282 --> 00:11:01,242
Oh, I'm sorry.
We don't discuss our process, ma'am.

166
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:04,245
When exactly did you learn
of your boyfriend's murder?

167
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:08,291
You want to know why I'm at work
the day my boyfriend is found dead.

168
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:12,003
- Why don't you just ask me?
- Okay.

169
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:15,173
Why are you at work the same day
your boyfriend is found dead?

170
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,258
I have patients who need me.

171
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:23,765
And if I had to sit at home and actually
think about Jim being gone...

172
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:24,974
...I'd lose it.

173
00:11:26,352 --> 00:11:31,147
Being here,
whether it looks good to you or not...

174
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:33,608
...is the only way
I know how to cope.

175
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:36,444
Are you all right?

176
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:40,156
- Yeah, I'm okay.
- No, he's been quite sick.

177
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:44,035
- Well, let me have a look at you.
- I'm fine.

178
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:45,787
Fever.

179
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:48,623
- Nausea, coughing?
- Oh, yeah.

180
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:49,958
Flu.

181
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,669
I'm not really supposed to do this,
but if you want...

182
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,463
...I can write a prescription
for an antiviral.

183
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:58,091
Sure.

184
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:06,349
Have this filled
and you will feel better in no time.

185
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:08,727
Sure. Thanks.

186
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,188
Thank you.

187
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,526
Any word from Gulbrand's partner?

188
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:19,654
Not much in the way of motive,
but he doesn't have an alibi.

189
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,656
Gulbrand's brother checked out.

190
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:24,367
Gretchen says he was with her
the night of the murder.

191
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:25,660
Roommate backs up the story.

192
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,706
- Are you still sick?
- Mm.

193
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,374
- Man, go see a doctor.
- I did.

194
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:34,252
The dead guy's girlfriend
wrote me a prescription.

195
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,922
- So go fill it.
- By the time I take it, I'll be better.

196
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,341
What did she give you, anyway?

197
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:49,142
"Oseltamivir phosphate."

198
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,854
May I see that?

199
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,276
Thank you.

200
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,779
Anything about this strike you as odd?

201
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:06,534
What's odd about it?
"Oseltamivir phosphate."

202
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:10,914
Exactly. When was the last time you saw
a doctor's handwriting you could read?

203
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:13,750
So she's precise.
Is that what you're implying?

204
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:18,254
Yes, and the possibility
that Dr. Brooke Harper is not a doctor.

205
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:20,715
Because she has penmanship skills?

206
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:24,219
And she doesn't have that cold,
creepy doctor-y vibe they all have.

207
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:26,638
Be fair.
Not all doctors are cold and creepy.

208
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:29,641
First day of school,
they get books and a dead human being.

209
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:34,896
That, I'm afraid, will change you.
Brooke Harper was warm and emotional.

210
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:38,399
You like her, so she can't be a doctor?

211
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:39,901
Pretty much.

212
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:44,239
The AMA and Boston General
both have records of a Brooke Harper.

213
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:45,615
See?

214
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,952
But it says here
that she's 64 years old.

215
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:51,579
Wow, she looks pretty good.

216
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:55,208
Is there a word for uncanny,
yet irritating?

217
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:04,467
Jeff, I'm going to be leaving
the clinic shortly...

218
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:06,761
...so this is going to be
our last session together.

219
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,346
Oh...

220
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:12,183
Oh, no, no, no. I need you, Dr. Harper.
How will I manage without you?

221
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,936
I'm sorry, Jeff.
I have enjoyed our sessions together.

222
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:18,439
I'm sure the clinic will provide you
with the best care possible.

223
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:23,611
But should you ever need
to speak with me personally...

224
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:24,946
...here's my private number.

225
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:30,451
I'm sorry to interrupt, Dr. Harper,
but the CBI are here again.

226
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:32,453
And they need to speak with you.

227
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:34,664
Tell them I'll be with them
in 10 minutes.

228
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,041
They say they need to speak
with you now.

229
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:39,460
This moment.
And they are most insistent.

230
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,964
All right, tell them I'll be right out,
Maggie. Thank you.

231
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:50,054
I mean, I just... I feel like I'm
on the verge of a real breakthrough.

232
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:54,809
I'm starting to open myself up again
to people in a real way.

233
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,896
My inner child is finally emerg...

234
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:01,649
Dr. Harper? Dr. Harper?

235
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:05,069
- Hey.
- Stop. You can't go in there.

236
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:10,491
Damn it. Let's go.

237
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,370
Um...

238
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:21,669
All I was able to find
at Dr. Brooke Harper's apartment.

239
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:24,047
Bank account emptied.
Credit cards maxed out.

240
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:27,467
She must have been packed
and ready to leave days ago.

241
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:30,845
Her social security number
and medical license are fakes too.

242
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:34,807
- We have no idea who this woman is.
- Well, we know that she's smart.

243
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:38,645
She posed as a doctor for seven months,
managed to elude you and Rigsby.

244
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:41,648
Well, she had a head start.
She didn't elude us.

245
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:44,525
All right, she eluded us.

246
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:47,862
She's a professional con woman.
I mean, she probably specializes...

247
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:51,532
...in the seduction of rich
and successful, socially-awkward men.

248
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,369
- You think she's done this before?
- Oh, yes. Many times.

249
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:56,913
Why kill Jim Gulbrand?
What's her motive?

250
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:59,707
- Maybe he found out the truth.
- Why not just vanish?

251
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,209
- Morning.
- Morning.

252
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:04,879
I've been going through Gulbrand's
financial records and found something.

253
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:08,216
Last year, Gulbrand made a series
of cash withdrawals...

254
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:10,885
...from various accounts
totaling $10 million.

255
00:16:11,553 --> 00:16:13,680
- What did he spend the money on?
- That's it.

256
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:16,349
He didn't deposit it.
Doesn't look like he spent it.

257
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:20,436
So either he paid somebody off
or he hid the money.

258
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:24,023
A cash nest egg, either from his ex-wife
or the SEC.

259
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,858
Maybe that's what Brooke was after.

260
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:28,403
If only we knew who she was
or where she was.

261
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:33,074
Well, we know that she's cool.
She's fearless. She's systematic.

262
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:36,911
She went back to the clinic for an extra
day to try and hook another sucker.

263
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,871
She's a planner.

264
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:43,251
Can we get a copy
of her last credit-card statement?

265
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,128
I can get it.

266
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:50,883
And they had the nerve to send me
a gold Mercedes instead of a black one...

267
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:52,593
...and so I sent it back.

268
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:54,387
Kathryn Gulbrand?

269
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:57,223
Kathryn Stubbs-Gulbrand
and you're interrupting.

270
00:16:57,391 --> 00:17:00,601
Ma'am, we have a few questions
regarding your ex-husband's death.

271
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:02,061
You wanna talk to me now?

272
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:05,565
Well, we could talk to you
at the station, if you'd prefer.

273
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:08,317
- Fine.
- Thank you. Thank you, ladies.

274
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,952
How long had you
and Jim Gulbrand been divorced?

275
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,121
Fourteen months.

276
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:21,622
That's when I moved out.

277
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,751
- The divorce was final a year ago.
- Were you angry?

278
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:27,628
Of course I was angry.
That's why people get divorced.

279
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:30,798
Court documents indicate
that you sued your ex-husband.

280
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,467
You bet your ass I did.

281
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:35,136
Jim tried to claim that the money
he had in stock...

282
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:37,638
...wasn't his,
but part of the company's capital.

283
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:41,601
I disagreed, and I won.
I got everything I wanted and more.

284
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:45,813
We believe that your ex-husband
may have hidden money...

285
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:48,649
...from you
during the divorce proceedings.

286
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:49,817
What?

287
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:52,445
He made $10 million
in cash withdrawals last year.

288
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:56,365
- You weren't aware of that?
- That son of a bitch. I knew it.

289
00:17:56,575 --> 00:17:58,284
I knew he was holding out.

290
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:01,162
- That wasn't a damn gym-locker key.
- What key?

291
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,956
Last year, he started wearing
this key around his neck.

292
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:07,168
I asked him what it was.
He said it was his gym-locker key...

293
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,462
...but I knew it wasn't. I knew it.

294
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,507
- How perceptive.
- What was that?

295
00:18:12,674 --> 00:18:15,510
- Nothing, ma'am.
- So you didn't know about the money?

296
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:18,137
If I did, it would be mine right now.

297
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,849
- Where is it?
- We don't know.

298
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:24,060
Half that money is legally mine.

299
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:26,687
I don't want Jim's brother
getting his hands on it.

300
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:28,981
I'm sure a judge will take care of it.

301
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:31,651
Last Friday, the night
of your ex-husband's murder...

302
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:34,028
...where were you from 7
through 10 p.m.?

303
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,572
I was at a wine tasting in Napa.

304
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,990
Can anyone confirm that?

305
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,701
Can you people charge me
with any crime?

306
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:43,412
- No, but...
- No. You can't.

307
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:46,749
When you can, maybe I'll tell you
the details of my personal life.

308
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:49,252
Until then, mind your own business.

309
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:56,175
I just got off the phone
with our liaison at the SEC.

310
00:18:56,343 --> 00:19:00,847
Turns out Jim Gulbrand was cooperating
with their investigation.

311
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,431
Rick Bregman never mentioned it.

312
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:04,684
Well, make sure you mention it to him.

313
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:06,269
What's this?

314
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:10,439
Brooke Harper only used the
credit card twice in the last two weeks.

315
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:13,860
This is what she bought
in one day of shopping, nine days ago...

316
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:16,654
...and this
is what she bought yesterday.

317
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:21,033
Now, what do these things tell us?
That's a wig, by the way.

318
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,744
- What's that in the bottom right?
- A bandage.

319
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:27,248
- Doesn't look like a bandage.
- It's a bandage.

320
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:31,752
- What do these things tell you?
- Brooke wanted to pose as a man?

321
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,755
- Right.
- But why? What's that other stuff?

322
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:36,757
Well, that's the puzzle.

323
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:42,430
That Kathryn Stubbs?
She's... She's an unhappy person.

324
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:45,308
- Where's Rigsby?
- He went to get his prescription filled.

325
00:19:45,475 --> 00:19:47,768
I think that Kathryn woman
made him worse.

326
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,312
She's hiding something too.

327
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:51,939
Wouldn't say who she was with
the night of the murder.

328
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:54,609
- Keep an eye on her.
- Interesting.

329
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,778
She did tell us Gulbrand
wore a key around his neck...

330
00:19:57,946 --> 00:19:59,822
...that he said was for his gym locker.

331
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:02,450
Only there wasn't a key
found on the body, was there?

332
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,619
- No.
- Aha.

333
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:07,788
She took his key.
That's why she dressed as a man.

334
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:11,292
So that she could get into his locker
in the changing room at the gym.

335
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:15,296
But if she had found Jim's millions,
she would have simply vanished.

336
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:18,299
- Why stick around?
- The money wasn't in the locker.

337
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:22,637
Exactly. She's now trying
to get inside somewhere else.

338
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,487
Thank you.

339
00:20:39,655 --> 00:20:41,364
Good afternoon. May I help you?

340
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,491
I'm Jim Gulbrand. I'm a member here.

341
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:47,787
Sir, I know Mr. Gulbrand well...

342
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:51,123
- ...and you are not he.
- What are you doing?

343
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,459
I'm confirming that Jim Gulbrand
is a member.

344
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:54,752
Why not just ask?

345
00:20:55,629 --> 00:20:58,047
- Go ahead, ask him.
- Is Jim Gulbrand a member here?

346
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,508
I'm sorry,
we don't divulge membership details.

347
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,510
- See?
- This is a murder investigation.

348
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,178
Mr. Gulbrand is dead.

349
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:07,390
- Oh, I'm very sorry to hear that.
- Well, thanks for your help.

350
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:10,559
Sir, this a private club.

351
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,561
What I'm learning...

352
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:18,859
...is that one can't just wander in here
and hang out. One needs a plan. Eh?

353
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:21,988
- We're gonna take a look around.
- That's not our policy, sir.

354
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:25,992
If we obtain a warrant, we're gonna
take every computer and piece of paper.

355
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:29,412
Then we're gonna have a sit-down chat
with each one of your members.

356
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,747
Welcome to the backgammon club.

357
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,499
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

358
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:46,554
I don't get it. What is she doing?

359
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:49,890
I don't know.
Maybe she likes the water.

360
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:53,728
- You feeling better?
- Yeah. Much.

361
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:57,106
It's weird. I know Brooke Harper's
not a real doctor...

362
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:59,692
...but whatever she gave me
really worked.

363
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:02,028
Good. I was getting worried
about you.

364
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,575
Hmm.

365
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,251
Grace.

366
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:21,422
- I've been thinking that maybe...
- Here we go.

367
00:22:30,557 --> 00:22:32,433
Rick Bregman.

368
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:39,357
- Hmm.
- The best friend and business partner.

369
00:22:41,401 --> 00:22:43,778
And lover of the ex-wife.

370
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:46,614
Apparently.

371
00:22:50,911 --> 00:22:52,328
Double?

372
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:54,747
No, you win.

373
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:57,792
Outrageous luck you have.
You are a monster.

374
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,878
- What is it now?
- What is it?

375
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:03,798
- Twenty thousand dollars.
- Twenty thousand dollars.

376
00:23:03,965 --> 00:23:06,592
- I must have my revenge.
- Well, if you insist.

377
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:08,135
- Jane.
- What?

378
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:10,805
- Want me to spell it?
- We're just having fun.

379
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:13,432
- Absolutely.
- First prince I've ever met.

380
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:16,268
- How sweet.
- Thank you.

381
00:23:20,982 --> 00:23:22,817
There she blows.

382
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:31,158
Prince, can I be excused
from this game? My date just arrived.

383
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:32,493
Of course.

384
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:36,038
- Maybe that's lucky for me, yeah?
- Probably.

385
00:23:36,623 --> 00:23:38,541
- Twenty thousand?
- Mm-hm.

386
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,335
Better enjoy.

387
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:47,341
- Hey, listen. Just forget about it, okay?
- Certainly not.

388
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:50,010
- You won fair and square.
- Well, actually, I cheated.

389
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:51,846
I controlled the dice.

390
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,433
It's in the wrist. Just in the wrist.

391
00:23:57,185 --> 00:24:00,479
I would have taken your money
and given it to a worthy cause...

392
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:03,524
...but my friend here
is a moralist of childish simplicity.

393
00:24:04,067 --> 00:24:05,943
Nice to meet you.

394
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:23,502
- Hello, gorgeous.
- Beat it, creep.

395
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:26,839
I'd call you by your real name,
but I don't know what it is.

396
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:28,883
Oh.

397
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:31,552
- Hello, Mr. Jane.
- Hi.

398
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:35,055
- I'm impressed. Well done.
- Oh, for finding you?

399
00:24:35,223 --> 00:24:36,474
Wasn't that difficult.

400
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:40,352
- Would you have a cigar?
- Thank you, no.

401
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,688
I hear they're not so good
for your health.

402
00:24:42,856 --> 00:24:45,941
- Well, who wants to live forever?
- It'd be horrible, wouldn't it?

403
00:24:46,109 --> 00:24:48,611
Immortality. Imagine the boredom.

404
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:53,073
My friend Cho here
will now take you by the wrist...

405
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:56,368
...so as not to let you
escape us again.

406
00:24:56,536 --> 00:24:58,787
- Hi.
- Warm hands.

407
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:01,790
I bet you say that
to all your arresting officers.

408
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:16,722
Who are you, Brooke?

409
00:25:17,390 --> 00:25:20,518
- How did you find me?
- Well, let's make a deal.

410
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:23,437
I'll tell you how we found you
if you tell us who you are.

411
00:25:23,605 --> 00:25:25,356
Okay.

412
00:25:25,524 --> 00:25:29,527
My name is Angela Dalibar and I'm from
Birmingham by way of Hong Kong.

413
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:34,114
- How did you find me?
- I planted a GPS tracking device on you.

414
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:38,202
Outstanding technology
No bigger than a stick of gum.

415
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,120
Tell us more about yourself, Angela.

416
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,956
How long have you been
a con woman?

417
00:25:42,123 --> 00:25:44,041
All my life, I suppose.

418
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:47,378
And I confess my name's
not really Angela.

419
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:50,047
And I didn't plant a GPS
tracking device on you.

420
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:52,424
How, then?

421
00:25:52,592 --> 00:25:56,136
Well, maybe you're not as enigmatic
and elusive as you think you are.

422
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:59,431
- I wouldn't be so sure of that.
- No?

423
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:03,143
You manipulate people
because you take pleasure in it.

424
00:26:03,311 --> 00:26:05,980
You enjoy being the smartest person
in the room.

425
00:26:06,147 --> 00:26:08,482
You're interested in money,
of course...

426
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:11,735
...but only so far as it allows you
to continue conning people.

427
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:16,740
You allow yourself one indulgence.
Not men, obviously.

428
00:26:16,908 --> 00:26:18,576
Not drinking, or drugs...

429
00:26:18,743 --> 00:26:21,662
...because you fear that they
will impair your abilities.

430
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:23,956
You move around too
much to have a pet...

431
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:27,960
chocolate.

432
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:31,463
You're good.

433
00:26:31,631 --> 00:26:34,842
So why do you do this, Brooke?
Neglected as a child?

434
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,761
Is this your way of getting attention?

435
00:26:38,638 --> 00:26:43,142
- Or is it something a little darker?
- Just a genuine mystery, I suppose.

436
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,769
We have your prints.
We'll know who you are soon.

437
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:49,607
Do you think one can ever truly
know another person?

438
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:50,858
I doubt it.

439
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:54,695
- How do you have Jim Gulbrand's key?
- He gave it to me.

440
00:26:54,863 --> 00:26:58,866
- Didn't tell you what it would unlock?
- It wasn't given as a key. It was symbol.

441
00:26:59,075 --> 00:27:01,535
Of our love.
It's the key to his heart.

442
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:06,081
You said "our love" with conviction.

443
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:08,834
Are you trying to tell us
you loved him too?

444
00:27:09,002 --> 00:27:11,545
Yes. To my great surprise.

445
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,465
I did come to love him, in a way.

446
00:27:15,091 --> 00:27:17,301
- He was a good, kind man.
- So sweet.

447
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:18,552
Yes, it is.

448
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:22,222
Yes, this is also the key to a locker
that holds $10 million.

449
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:24,725
Really? I thought it was for cigars.

450
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:26,977
- I love a good cigar.
- Nope.

451
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:30,689
- Ten million dollars.
- But that's just silly.

452
00:27:30,857 --> 00:27:33,359
Why would Jim
keep $10 million in a locker?

453
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:36,904
- She's good.
- Yeah, she is.

454
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:42,576
- What are you doing here?
- Duh, looking for the money.

455
00:27:42,744 --> 00:27:46,038
Rick figured maybe there were
secret compartments on the boat.

456
00:27:46,998 --> 00:27:49,208
How long have you been seeing
Rick Bregman?

457
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:51,085
About a year.

458
00:27:51,252 --> 00:27:53,587
You were divorced from Jim Gulbrand
a year ago.

459
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:56,715
Were you and Rick involved
while you were still married?

460
00:27:56,883 --> 00:27:58,258
Involved?

461
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:01,845
Were you having sexual intercourse
with him?

462
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:05,099
- No. Rick would never do that to Jim.
- But you would.

463
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:09,228
I have needs just like anybody else.
I refuse to be ashamed of my needs.

464
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:12,022
Why did you lie to us
about your relationship?

465
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:13,565
I knew how it would look.

466
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:16,026
Knew it would make you look guilty
of murder?

467
00:28:16,194 --> 00:28:19,196
No. Yes. It's just...

468
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:24,118
It wasn't just that. Gaia Matrix's
stock has been falling for months.

469
00:28:24,285 --> 00:28:26,704
This market has hurt
even the best of companies.

470
00:28:26,871 --> 00:28:30,290
Last thing I need is some Page Six
sex scandal to make things worse.

471
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:33,043
So you misled us
in order to protect your money?

472
00:28:33,211 --> 00:28:36,630
I misled you to protect the company
Jim and I built from the ground up.

473
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:39,717
Were you aware Jim
was cooperating with SEC investigators?

474
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:43,971
- Jim would never go behind my back.
- Well, he would and he did.

475
00:28:44,180 --> 00:28:47,641
The question is if you found out,
what would you do to stop him?

476
00:28:49,310 --> 00:28:50,978
This conversation is over.

477
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:55,607
When did you find out about
the $10 million he was hiding?

478
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:57,651
Over.

479
00:29:03,074 --> 00:29:04,825
Ten million dollars?

480
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:06,660
- That's a lot of money.
- Oh, yeah.

481
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:09,163
Jim trusted you
with the security of his company.

482
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:12,833
He valued your
outside-the-box thinking.

483
00:29:13,001 --> 00:29:16,295
You advised him on what to do
with the money, didn't you?

484
00:29:16,796 --> 00:29:17,838
Didn't you?

485
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:21,467
We don't care if hiding the money
was illegal or unethical.

486
00:29:21,634 --> 00:29:25,471
- Our focus is the homicide investigation.
- No, it's not that.

487
00:29:25,638 --> 00:29:27,639
It's just...

488
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:31,685
I absolutely promised Jim
I wouldn't say anything.

489
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:35,314
We found out Jim's girlfriend,
Brooke Harper, is a con woman.

490
00:29:35,815 --> 00:29:39,234
We think she was after the money
and might have murdered Jim to get it.

491
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,528
We found her along with this key...

492
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:45,699
...trying to open Gulbrand's cabinet
at the backgammon club.

493
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,952
Key didn't work.
Evidently she took it from Jim...

494
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:50,954
...but doesn't know
where the money is.

495
00:29:51,122 --> 00:29:54,124
- That's some lady.
- Oh, yeah.

496
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:57,711
If you help us find the money,
we can prove Brooke was looking for it...

497
00:29:57,879 --> 00:30:00,964
- ...and establish a motive for murder.
- So Stuart?

498
00:30:01,132 --> 00:30:04,885
- Do you know where the money is?
- No.

499
00:30:05,386 --> 00:30:07,805
Not exactly, anyway.

500
00:30:07,972 --> 00:30:11,975
Jim did come to me for some
out-of-the-box security advice...

501
00:30:12,143 --> 00:30:15,145
...like you said. He wanted to hide
the money from his ex-wife.

502
00:30:15,313 --> 00:30:19,066
I told him safety-deposit boxes and
offshore accounts could be traced easily.

503
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:22,152
- They wouldn't be of any use.
- Where'd you tell him to hide?

504
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:25,030
Off the grid.
Out of the financial institutions.

505
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:27,199
Any place a trail
couldn't be established.

506
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:28,659
Like a home safe?

507
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,203
No. Anything on his property
is subject to search.

508
00:30:31,371 --> 00:30:34,331
No. It had to be secure, obviously,
hence the key.

509
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:37,751
More importantly, it had to be
a place no one would think to look.

510
00:30:37,919 --> 00:30:40,254
- Hidden in plain sight.
- Yes.

511
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:42,339
That's my involvement.
I have no idea...

512
00:30:42,507 --> 00:30:44,424
- ...where he actually hid the money.
- I see.

513
00:30:45,802 --> 00:30:47,302
Oops.

514
00:30:48,054 --> 00:30:50,180
Oopsie.

515
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:54,101
Don't wanna go losing that,
now, do we?

516
00:30:55,895 --> 00:30:57,104
What do you make of it?

517
00:30:57,272 --> 00:30:59,231
Think he knows where Jim
hid the money?

518
00:30:59,399 --> 00:31:01,692
He knows the general
whereabouts of the money...

519
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,694
...but he doesn't know exactly.

520
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:07,948
And the devil is in the details,
isn't he?

521
00:31:19,419 --> 00:31:20,460
Here's what happened.

522
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:22,796
I'm all ears.

523
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:26,216
Two weeks ago, you took the locker key
from around Jim's neck...

524
00:31:26,384 --> 00:31:29,469
...when he was sleeping
and replaced it with an identical one...

525
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:31,305
...so Jim was none the wiser.

526
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:35,809
Then, when you tried to open the
locker at the gym, the key didn't fit.

527
00:31:35,977 --> 00:31:37,895
So the money was hidden
somewhere else.

528
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:40,898
Last Friday, you got impatient...

529
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:44,067
...and you pushed Jim to tell you
where he'd hidden the money.

530
00:31:44,235 --> 00:31:47,237
Jim wouldn't tell you,
you got mad, and you killed him.

531
00:31:47,822 --> 00:31:48,906
No.

532
00:31:49,115 --> 00:31:51,658
You probably didn't do it on purpose,
did you?

533
00:31:51,868 --> 00:31:53,952
- It was an accident.
- It wasn't.

534
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,370
I didn't do it.

535
00:31:57,332 --> 00:32:01,293
Sad thing is, with all your skills...

536
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:05,380
...the answer was right there
in front of you. You just didn't see it.

537
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,969
You didn't do enough research.

538
00:32:11,262 --> 00:32:14,806
You're playing me.
You don't know either.

539
00:32:14,974 --> 00:32:18,143
Jim's security systems were all designed
by the same man.

540
00:32:18,311 --> 00:32:20,145
- Stuart Hansen?
- Him.

541
00:32:20,313 --> 00:32:22,105
He suggested
where to put the money.

542
00:32:22,273 --> 00:32:25,859
You could have squeezed the truth
out of him very swiftly, I imagine.

543
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:30,280
Putty to a woman like you.
But instead, you had to kill a man.

544
00:32:30,490 --> 00:32:34,660
I wouldn't do that.
You don't know me.

545
00:32:34,827 --> 00:32:36,370
Lindsey Smith from San Diego.

546
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:42,876
Father, Ryan, a salesman.
Mother, Debbie, homemaker.

547
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:46,713
Two Miss Teen
Temecula County titles. Wow.

548
00:32:47,215 --> 00:32:52,344
Varsity softball. Church-choir soloist.

549
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:55,389
Then you disappeared off the records
for a couple of years.

550
00:32:55,556 --> 00:32:56,848
And when you came back...

551
00:32:57,016 --> 00:33:00,852
...you're a con artist
with two fraud convictions.

552
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:10,153
- What happened?
- Nothing happened.

553
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:13,573
I like money and I'm easily bored.

554
00:33:14,742 --> 00:33:17,452
There's gotta be more to it than that.

555
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:20,580
It's a cold, hard lonely life you lead.

556
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,334
What is it that drives you?

557
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:28,088
Passion for excellence.

558
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:36,555
Okay.

559
00:33:36,889 --> 00:33:39,766
Relax a while.
An agent will be in here...

560
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:43,353
...to run you through
the formal charges against you.

561
00:33:43,896 --> 00:33:45,522
Run away.

562
00:33:46,065 --> 00:33:48,108
Good luck, Lindsey.

563
00:33:48,943 --> 00:33:50,527
And to you.

564
00:33:58,703 --> 00:33:59,745
Right. Right.

565
00:33:59,912 --> 00:34:01,955
Any luck with Harper?

566
00:34:02,123 --> 00:34:03,623
There's no luck involved.

567
00:34:03,791 --> 00:34:05,584
- Outcome's a given.
- Is that so?

568
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:09,129
Yeah. It's all applied psychology
and Newtonian physics.

569
00:34:32,236 --> 00:34:34,154
Excuse me, can I see some ID, please?

570
00:34:34,322 --> 00:34:36,573
You call that a uniform shirt?
It's filthy.

571
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:40,410
- Well, I tried to clean it...
- Filthy. No excuses, Stiles.

572
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:44,915
I'll address this matter with your captain
at my earliest convenience.

573
00:34:57,386 --> 00:34:58,428
- Really?
- Yeah.

574
00:34:58,596 --> 00:35:00,388
I'm gonna make up a list for you.

575
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:01,598
She on the move yet?

576
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:04,392
She made one stop
and hasn't left her motel room since.

577
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:06,603
- What did she stop for?
- Chocolate.

578
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:09,689
And thank you.

579
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:13,276
- For what?
- For just letting us play it out like this.

580
00:35:13,820 --> 00:35:16,029
We would have had to let her go anyway.

581
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:18,281
Nothing to keep her on
until we get proof.

582
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:19,950
Besides, this is a simple plan.

583
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:23,370
It's when you start getting costumes
and props that I get nervous.

584
00:35:23,538 --> 00:35:26,706
Trick plays like this?
My dad calls them chewing-gum plays.

585
00:35:26,874 --> 00:35:30,710
Sometimes, you fool the other guy.
Sometimes, you get gum in your hair.

586
00:35:30,878 --> 00:35:32,170
She's moving.

587
00:35:38,594 --> 00:35:42,264
Train station. It had to be a train station.

588
00:35:42,431 --> 00:35:44,141
What's wrong with a train station?

589
00:35:44,308 --> 00:35:46,434
People, noise, tunnels, trains.
More people.

590
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:51,731
Her vehicle is stopped
outside the station.

591
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:54,818
Hold your
positions until I give you the word.

592
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:56,111
Yes, boss. Standing by.

593
00:35:58,072 --> 00:35:59,573
Copy that.

594
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:01,950
South to Flagstaff is now boarding.

595
00:36:04,745 --> 00:36:06,329
All set.

596
00:36:09,917 --> 00:36:11,334
Chewing-gum plays.

597
00:36:11,544 --> 00:36:13,753
I can see my hair
with a big chunk out of it.

598
00:36:13,921 --> 00:36:17,174
You'd look good with short hair.
Choppy, all kind of Peter Pan.

599
00:36:17,341 --> 00:36:19,092
- Good for the eyes.
- Okay, heads up.

600
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:21,678
She's in motion
approaching the station now.

601
00:36:21,846 --> 00:36:23,263
Cho, do you have a visual?

602
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,935
Affirmative.
She's exiting the vehicle now.

603
00:36:41,324 --> 00:36:43,074
She has Stuart Hansen with her.

604
00:36:46,829 --> 00:36:50,624
She has a gun. Be advised.
Brooke Harper is armed.

605
00:36:54,128 --> 00:36:55,962
Rigsby, Van Pelt, what's your status?

606
00:36:56,130 --> 00:36:59,466
I have Harper and Hansen in sight.
Van Pelt, she's moving your way.

607
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:03,887
Got them. Looks like she's headed
to the commuter lockers. I'm on it.

608
00:37:21,989 --> 00:37:26,201
Thirty-six San Diego local
will not be stopping in Santa Barbara.

609
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:28,745
It's the gate. I'm stuck.

610
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:33,166
All right. Don't move.
Don't do anything. Don't say anything.

611
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:35,001
This better be the right place.

612
00:37:49,517 --> 00:37:51,768
She opened a locker.
I think she has the money.

613
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:56,523
- Okay...
- Wait. Just wait a moment.

614
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:05,865
Oh, my.

615
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:10,078
Don't move or I'll kill you.

616
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:22,549
Don't move.

617
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:33,435
- Don't even think about it, Hansen.
- I got it. It's cool.

618
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,729
Done.

619
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:47,991
You're under arrest, again.

620
00:38:52,997 --> 00:38:54,706
Come on, let's go.

621
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,752
- You good?
- Yeah.

622
00:39:03,591 --> 00:39:06,301
Jason Bradshaw. Jason Wade.

623
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:10,430
Anthony Wade. Anthony Samuels.
The list goes on.

624
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:12,682
All aliases you've used in scams...

625
00:39:12,850 --> 00:39:15,477
...ranging from identity theft
to Ponzi schemes.

626
00:39:16,103 --> 00:39:18,271
- You're quite the virtuoso.
- Thank you.

627
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:23,443
But this one, this would have been your
most daring and successful crime yet.

628
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:27,113
Ten million dollars
of Jim Gulbrand's money.

629
00:39:28,449 --> 00:39:30,367
Gulbrand was the perfect mark.

630
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:33,661
Rich, liquid and unconventional.

631
00:39:33,829 --> 00:39:36,164
I bet he didn't
even check your references.

632
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:39,000
Nothing says trustworthy like a wheelchair.

633
00:39:40,461 --> 00:39:42,462
You convinced Gulbrand
that the station...

634
00:39:42,630 --> 00:39:44,756
...was the genius place
to hide his money.

635
00:39:46,258 --> 00:39:49,677
Screw orthodox wisdom.
Think sideways, right?

636
00:39:50,513 --> 00:39:51,805
Right?

637
00:39:51,972 --> 00:39:56,017
And he ate it up. He ate it up.
Why wouldn't he?

638
00:39:56,769 --> 00:39:59,145
Then you simply needed
to get the key.

639
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:07,695
You went to the yacht that night
because you knew he'd be alone.

640
00:40:15,204 --> 00:40:18,581
You also knew
he kept the key with him.

641
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:24,421
You did what needed to be done.
You killed Jim Gulbrand...

642
00:40:24,588 --> 00:40:27,006
...and you got rid of the body.

643
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:44,023
But you didn't count
on Brooke Harper.

644
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:47,610
You couldn't have known
she swapped the real key...

645
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:49,112
...with a look-alike.

646
00:40:49,321 --> 00:40:53,366
You didn't realize anything was wrong
until you tried to open the locker.

647
00:40:53,868 --> 00:41:00,039
It wasn't until we came to Gaia Matrix
with a real key...

648
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:02,375
...that it dawned on you
what she'd done.

649
00:41:02,543 --> 00:41:05,211
I can only imagine your surprise.

650
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:08,381
Six months of living in that chair.

651
00:41:09,633 --> 00:41:12,635
Six months and no one
ever questioned me about it.

652
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:13,970
Why did you?

653
00:41:14,763 --> 00:41:16,556
When I meet someone
in a wheelchair...

654
00:41:16,724 --> 00:41:19,726
...I check the bottoms of their shoes.

655
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:29,652
The bottoms of your shoes
were scuffed.

656
00:41:33,574 --> 00:41:37,911
I've been checking shoes for years.
This is the first time it's ever paid off.

657
00:41:38,078 --> 00:41:41,998
That's gratifying, man.
Very, very gratifying.

658
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:50,089
He's a pistol, isn't he?

659
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:03,186
Sorry about the cuffs.

660
00:42:04,188 --> 00:42:06,314
- My own fault.
- Oh, yeah.

661
00:42:09,318 --> 00:42:11,778
I wish I could let you go again,
but, you know...

662
00:42:12,988 --> 00:42:14,322
I understand.

663
00:42:15,407 --> 00:42:17,992
That urge you have
to get one over on people...

664
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:21,788
...the need to be smarter
than the next guy?

665
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:27,794
- It'll keep biting you on the ass.
- So my butt'll hurt occasionally.

666
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:30,463
I'll still be smarter than the next guy.

667
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:35,009
Brooke Harper?

668
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:37,929
No. Jessica Waters.
That's Harper right there.

669
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:42,934
Agent, this is Harper.

670
00:42:44,144 --> 00:42:45,728
- Worth a try.
- Of course.

671
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:47,647
Brooke Harper, I'm Agent Fred Hayes.

672
00:42:47,815 --> 00:42:52,360
I'll be in charge of transporting you
to the Federal Detention Center in Davis.

673
00:42:54,446 --> 00:42:56,030
Let's go.

674
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:02,579
See you around, Patrick.

675
00:43:03,872 --> 00:43:07,000
I doubt you'll being seeing
much of anybody for a few years.

676
00:43:07,167 --> 00:43:09,002
I don't know about that, Agent Hayes.

677
00:43:09,169 --> 00:43:11,838
She's very good at what she does.

678
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:14,966
Yeah.

